@ 17.10.1.4 - Proto-Indo-Aryan to Western Middle Indo-Aryan
# citation: Pogostick Man, from Shukla, Shaligram (1974), “Phonological change and dialect
# 			variation in Middle-Indo-Aryan”. In Anderson, J., and C. Jones (Eds.), Historical
# 			Linguistics II:391-401.
	C(C) > ∅ / C_#
	VN VC:[- nasal] > V:[+ nasal] V:[+ long] / _#
	a{i,j}(a) a{u,w}(a) > e o
	j w > d͡ʒ b / V_V
	C > C:[+ voice] / V_V
	{bʱ,dʱ,ɡʱ} {j,v} > h ∅ / V_V
	Vm > Vv / _V
	Vv > V:[+ nasal]v / _V
	e o > i u / _#
	V:[+ long] > V:[- long] / _#
	ah > o
	ɽ > i
	kʂ > t͡ʃ:[+ long]
	{ʂ,ç} > s
	tv dv > p b
	C₁C₂ > C₂C₂ / V_V
	Cn > CC / V_V // C = d͡ʒ
	d͡ʒɲ > ɳ:[+ long] / V_V